In `QtileState.apply`, the first `try/except` around updating `qtile.groups_map[group]` catches `KeyError` when a saved group name is missing, and the test data includes `"missing_new"` which is not initially in `groups_map`. Later, the screen-assignment loop catches `(KeyError, IndexError)`: `"missing_group"` causes a caught `KeyError` when looking up `qtile.groups_map[group]`, and screen index `4` causes a caught `IndexError` when indexing `qtile.screens` for a qtile with only two screens. Considering exception kinds in first-seen order and deduplicating repeated `KeyError`, the caught kinds are `KeyError` then `IndexError`.

## Answer
{"caught_exception_kinds":["KeyError","IndexError"]}
